# download-runner build context .dockerignore (issue #439). Same intent as the
# repo-root .dockerignore's comment: a miss here ships the file INTO the image
# layer, which is worse than a git miss. This context must never bake in the
# account-gated vcf-download-tool/UMDS installers, depot tokens, activation
# codes, or any operator credential (ADR-0015 — those are operator-installed
# managed state on a persistent volume, not build inputs).

.git/
.github/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Vendor installer packages, depot tokens/activation codes, operator config —
# must never reach this build context even if accidentally placed alongside
# it during development. Mirrors the sibling repo's own artifacts by name so
# a careless `cp -r` of the sibling checkout into this directory can't leak
# them into the image.
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.gz
downloadToken.txt
softwareDepotActivationCode.txt
downloadConfig.xml
*.token
*.vault
vault-pass*
secrets*.json
secrets*.yml
*.local.json
*.local.yml
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
.env
.env.*

# Build/test output not needed inside the image.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
